{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:links.29", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer.1", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer/field:delivery-id.1", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer/field:delivery-tag.1", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer/field:message-format.1"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "the split that is one cut too far: the same octets, offered as a continuation of a delivery that has already completed, are refused because there is no delivery for them to continue \u2014 the `more` flag's other half, which a family that only ever admits framings cannot show", "start": "session:MAPPED", "steps": [{"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 18}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "link", "type": "string"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "boolean", "value": true}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000001d02000001005312c0100aa1046c696e6b434240404040404043", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001d02000001005313c010074370000003e84370000003e8434343", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000002702000001005314c00b064343a003746167434041005375a00a667261676d656e746564", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001e02000001005314c0020143005377a10a667261676d656e746564", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000002302000001005314c00706434040404041005377a10a667261676d656e746564", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:invalid-field", "reason": "malformed", "state": "session:DISCARDING", "status": "refused"}, "note": "`more` was unset on the transfer that completed the delivery, so this one begins another: a delivery that begins without a delivery-id, a delivery-tag and a message-format is what those three clauses refuse, and no continuation of the finished delivery exists for these octets to continue"}], "vector": "flow-negative-transfer-after-the-message-ended"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:links.29", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:open/field:max-frame-size.1", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:open/field:max-frame-size.2", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:connections.1", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer.1"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "the clause's own subject: `links.29` allows a message to be split because it is too large for one frame, and the size it defers to is the peer's announced maximum \u2014 so a split point that fits is admitted and one that does not is refused, in one vector, from one sender, on one link", "start": "connection:START", "steps": [{"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}, {"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:OPEN_PIPE", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 16}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "client", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 512}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 0, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:OPEN_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001f02000000005310c01204a1067365727665724070ffffffff60ffff", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:OPENED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:BEGIN_SENT", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 17}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"type": "null"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "uint", "value": 1000}, {"type": "uint", "value": 1000}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000001c02000001005311c00f046000014370000003e870000003e8", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 18}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "link", "type": "string"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "boolean", "value": true}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000001d02000001005312c0100aa1046c696e6b434240404040404043", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001d02000001005313c010074370000003e84370000003e8434343", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000005402000001005314c0020143766520746f2066697420696e206f6e65206672616d652c2061206d65737361676520646f6573206e6f74206861766520746f2066697420696e206f6e65206672616d652c20", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:connection:framing-error", "reason": "limit", "state": "connection:DISCARDING", "status": "refused"}, "note": "this peer announced a maximum frame size of 512, and the first frame of this delivery would total 513: one octet over the limit, which is the smallest framing the artifact refuses. The split at 487 two steps above is the same sender, the same message and the same single cut with one octet less in the first frame, and it is admitted \u2014 which is what makes this a limit on the framing rather than on fragmentation"}], "vector": "flow-negative-fragment-over-the-announced-frame-size"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:links.29", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer.1", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer/field:delivery-id.1", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer/field:delivery-id.u1"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "a legitimate two-transfer framing of the message, followed by a continuation whose delivery-id contradicts the first transfer's. The step above shows the same framing admitted with the field omitted (`delivery-id.1` lets a continuation omit it); carrying a *different* value is the error, and both artefacts must refuse it with amqp:invalid-field and the malformed class", "start": "session:MAPPED", "steps": [{"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 18}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "link", "type": "string"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "boolean", "value": true}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000001d02000001005312c0100aa1046c696e6b434240404040404043", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001d02000001005313c010074370000003e84370000003e8434343", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000002202000001005314c00b064343a003746167434041005375a00a667261676d", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001e02000001005314c00706434040404041656e746564005377a10a", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001f02000001005314c0080643520140404041667261676d656e746564", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:invalid-field", "reason": "malformed", "state": "session:DISCARDING", "status": "refused"}, "note": "the third transfer of this delivery carries delivery-id again, with a value the first transfer's does not have: `delivery-id.u1` says \"It is an error if the delivery-id on a continuation transfer differs from the delivery-id on the first transfer of a delivery\""}], "vector": "flow-negative-continuation-delivery-id-differs"}
